    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Card: Global.Text 71769, 74322, icon 9553 (the fork battle's own ids)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: the scene wc_sweetwater_climb needs one native load with this roster. The fork's scene layout, not a captured one; local kinds take ids 14029*100+n; knockouts, score, coins and the level gate are the fork fights' (fights/14xxx.json); job XP is the battles' 50."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) 1 later group(s) of the fork come as waves at their own spots: the first when the guards are down, each next one when the one before is down or 16 s after it (the captured Frostfang battle's gap)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) The guide's main goal is the one goal shown from the start and is done when the boss falls; the boss waits, dormant, for the waves. The results follow the exit door, which opens with the main goal."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Built by scripts/dungeon_fights.py from data/content/dungeons/sweetwater_climb.json, its notes page and the fork battle; under the id (14029) quests name."
    },
    {"kind": "wiki", "evidence": "L1194 (owner 2026-11-12: the end-of-battle prize wheel depends on the player's class): the wheel is this battle's own fanbyte page 'FR Place:Sweetwater Climb' (Prize Wheel Rewards, one list per class plus its General Purpose part; cached lab/references/fanbyte-battles-20261112/FR_Place_Sweetwater_Climb.html). Each class's wheel holds its own items and the shared items; the coins are the page's. It replaces every earlier note in this record about the prize wheel or its prizes."}
